Esoterica's likeness on the sealed door of the heptagonal chamber beneath the [[Geography/Færrin/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] is a creature almost completely covered by a dark, flowing robe, its too many gray arms sticking out at odd angles, each hand holding a different spellcasting focus: a wand, a staff, a crystal orb, a reliquary, some goat entrails, and a bone flute. A single green-glowing eye peeks from the darkness of the robe. Behind the door lies a haberdasher.

His own body is another thing. At the heart of the wreck of the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid|Hesperid]], in the old engine room where the ship struck him, he is a figure of golden light with three giant heads and six arms, each hand holding a different implement of magic, and a giant chain wound a few times about him, ending in an anchor driven into the centre of his body. The chain does not check him.

[[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] knows him by another name: Gremory, a fourth-generation Thessian. He was one of the weaker ones, and his one subject was magic, at which he grew very good. A Sedecium crew tracked him to the Hesperid on the eve of his ascent and ran their ship into him to stop it. The collision cut the ship nearly in half and failed; Gremory rose, and he has sat at the wreck's heart since, the beat that turns it.
